WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:04.224
Legal teams work across agreements, amendments, correspondence, policies and
exhibits.

00:04.224 --> 00:13.133
Before advice is formed or a position is approved, the lawyer needs the
governing clause, the relevant version and a clear route back

00:13.133 --> 00:14.295
to the record.

00:14.295 --> 00:22.043
When the matter set is complex, experienced people spend time reconstructing
relationships that should be visible at the point of

00:22.043 --> 00:22.430
review.

00:23.430 --> 00:31.159
The apparent answer may sit in the main agreement, an amendment, a schedule,
later correspondence or an incorporated policy.

00:31.159 --> 00:33.193
A defined term can change.

00:33.193 --> 00:35.227
A clause can be replaced.

00:35.227 --> 00:38.888
A document can apply only from a particular date.

00:38.888 --> 00:41.735
The challenge is not simply retrieving text.

00:41.735 --> 00:47.430
It is identifying the relationships, chronology and authority that a human
reviewer must assess.

00:48.430 --> 00:54.670
Cortessa's target legal-site deployment gives each authorised professional a
dedicated, self-sufficient box.

00:54.670 --> 01:01.950
Permitted matter documents, ingestion, index, on-device model and source
viewer remain on that box.

01:01.950 --> 01:07.150
Audit and Ask run locally against the approved matter corpus.

01:07.150 --> 01:11.310
Author remains in development and requires further testing.

01:11.310 --> 01:16.510
The lawyer controls access, context, interpretation and every approved
revision.

01:17.510 --> 01:25.171
Professional boxes are designed to connect through permission-scoped
departmental nodes for matter teams, knowledge and legal

01:25.171 --> 01:29.959
operations, then to an on-site hub inside the air-gapped site.

01:29.959 --> 01:36.184
Matter permissions and selected sharing remain explicit; the architecture
never implies cross-client access.

01:36.184 --> 01:40.494
This is the target architecture, not a deployed-network claim.

01:40.494 --> 01:47.197
The offline contract and application foundations exist; authenticated
transport, key operations, scheduling, backup, recovery,

01:47.197 --> 01:50.070
assurance and rollout remain deployment work.

01:51.070 --> 01:54.194
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

01:54.194 --> 02:03.176
Across the bounded matter set, it can surface an amendment that appears to
replace a clause, an exhibit that cites a missing source,

02:03.176 --> 02:06.690
inconsistent defined terms, uncertain dates or a broken reference.

02:06.690 --> 02:10.205
Each candidate enters legal review as a documentary question.

02:10.205 --> 02:14.110
It is not legal advice or a concluded legal finding.

02:15.110 --> 02:20.756
Each audit result leads back to the document and passage that created it.

02:20.756 --> 02:27.270
The lawyer can open the source, inspect the surrounding clause and assess
chronology and hierarchy.

02:27.270 --> 02:32.916
If the evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:32.916 --> 02:40.733
The legal reviewer determines significance, accepts or rejects the candidate,
and records the outcome through the existing process.

02:40.733 --> 02:45.510
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish interpretation or legal
accuracy.

02:46.510 --> 02:53.707
Client instructions, legal context, professional duties and strategic
consequences cannot be delegated to a language model.

02:53.707 --> 02:57.305
Cortessa can expose the evidence route and uncertainty.

02:57.305 --> 03:03.603
A qualified lawyer decides what governs, what it means and what action is
appropriate.

03:03.603 --> 03:10.350
Cortessa does not replace a solicitor, form a legal position, decide privilege
or determine disclosure.

03:11.350 --> 03:19.410
An approved revision can carry signed identity, content hash, parent lineage
and approved audit context through its permission-scoped

03:19.410 --> 03:22.992
team node and, where authorised, the on-site hub.

03:22.992 --> 03:27.917
Conflicts remain explicit; the hub cannot decide legal meaning or disclosure.

03:27.917 --> 03:33.290
Receipt does not establish privilege, certify accuracy or automatically index
a document.

03:33.290 --> 03:41.350
The receiving professional governs import and use, while the local Ledger
supports inspection without replacing the legal file.

03:42.350 --> 03:45.629
Compare matched tasks against the current workflow.

03:45.629 --> 03:52.654
Measure time to the relevant clause, citation completeness, amendment
visibility, correct refusals, reviewer effort and

03:52.654 --> 03:53.122
reproducibility.

03:53.122 --> 03:56.869
Include ambiguous drafting, missing documents and conflicting provisions.

03:56.869 --> 03:59.679
Record corpus preparation and setup effort.

03:59.679 --> 04:08.110
The result should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any broader evaluation.

04:09.110 --> 04:14.074
Bring one closed, controlled matter set and the authorised legal
professionals.

04:14.074 --> 04:18.587
Test the evidence route and permissioned team exchange before expansion.

04:18.587 --> 04:23.551
Cortessa claims no legal deployment, privilege determination or completed site
rollout.

04:23.551 --> 04:26.710
Start a conversation about a scoped evaluation.
